<h2>Segment 239 &mdash; karma and the two worlds</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s239S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239q1">ji skad du</span>, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w1">sems can</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w2">las</span> kyi <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s239w3">dbang gis</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w4">ri</span>, , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w5">nag po</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w6">dus</span> su <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w7">skyes</span> te dper, , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w8">sems dmyal</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w9">mtho ris</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w10">&#x27;jig rten</span> du, , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w11">mtshon</span> dang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w12">rin chen</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w13">shing</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w14">bzhin</span> no, , zhes gsungs so, , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w15">&#x27;jig rten</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w16">gnyis</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w17">thun mong</span> gi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w18">las</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w19">yin <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s239m19">min</span></span> gnyis kyis <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w20">bskyed pa</span> ni, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w21"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s239m21">sems</span> tsam</span> gyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w22">gzhung</span> du <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s239w23">yang</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w24">bshad</span> pas <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w25"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s239m25">sems</span> tsam</span> gyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w26">lugs</span> la&#x27;ang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w27">snod kyi &#x27;jig rten</span> med pa min no</span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s239S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239q1">As the verse goes</span>, It&#x27;s <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s239w3">through</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w2">karma</span> of <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w1">living beings</span> That the great <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w5">dark</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w4">mountains</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w7">arise</span> in their <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w6">time</span>. It&#x27;s <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w14">like</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w8">hells</span>, and the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w9">heavens above</span>, And <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w11">swords</span>, and <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w12">jewels</span>, and <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w13">trees</span> in the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w10">world</span>. The great <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w22">books</span> of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w21"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s239m21">Mind</span>-Only School</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s239w23">also</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w24">discuss</span> whether the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w16">two</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w15">worlds</span> [of beings and the place they live] are <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w20">produced</span> by <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w18">karma</span> that is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w17">collective</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w19">or <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s239m19">not</span></span>, and so it&#x27;s not as though the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w26">system</span> of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w25"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s239m25">Mind</span> Only</span> denies the existence of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s239w27">world where beings live</span>.</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex, reconciliation of independent Tibetan-first and English-first proposals. The verse is translation. ri/mountains, nag po/dark, dus/time, rin chen/jewels and shing/trees record overt lexical exponents only. They do not assert that dark modifies mountains in Tibetan or that rin chen shing coordinates two objects: ILL:2684 instead reads days of darkness and trees made of jewel. The single like is assigned to final bzhin; initial dper shares the comparison frame and is omitted. The first world is the verse occurrence, worlds the second source occurrence; the two-world bracketed explanation is supplied apparatus and remains unwrapped. thun mong/collective and las/karma remain separate atoms in the relative-clause recast; supplied that is remains unwrapped. HGM yin min owns or not, with min/not inside it. HGM sems tsam licenses both complete school names, with sems/Mind inside each. The final snod kyi 'jig rten owns the established world where beings live. med pa min no is a distributed double negation: no independent denies or existence predicate is banked, and the full explanatory English sentence is not captured. No null is used for uncertainty or distributed meaning.</div>
